I cannot reproduce the outage. End-to-end reachability between racks is currently healthy. Cross-rack pings succeed both ways (pc_0_0 → pc_0_1 and pc_0_1 → pc_0_0) with 0% loss and low RTT. Both hosts have correct IPs and default gateways (pc_0_0 via 10.0.0.1, pc_0_1 via 10.0.1.1). In the fabric, all BGP sessions are established and exchanging prefixes: leaf_router_0_0 (AS 65200) peers with both spines (AS 65100/65101) and receives one prefix from each; leaf_router_0_1 (AS 65201) shows the same. The spines and super_spine_router_0 (AS 65000) have active adjacencies and are advertising/receiving the expected routes. This indicates the leaf–spine–super-spine path between racks is operational.

Affected component: None at present; the routing/control-plane (FRR/BGP) and data-plane links are working.

Mechanism: With BGP adjacencies up and host defaults set, traffic is correctly routed across the CLOS fabric, so inter-rack connectivity functions as expected.

Localization: Verified on pc_0_0, pc_0_1, leaf_router_0_0, leaf_router_0_1, spine_router_0_0, spine_router_0_1, and super_spine_router_0.

Root cause: No fault found; the reported outage is not reproducible and was likely transient or already resolved.

Corrective fix: No changes required. Recommend monitoring; if the issue recurs, capture timestamps, traceroute from the affected host, and “show bgp summary” on the nearest leaf to pinpoint any intermittent session or link flaps. 
